@author "Claude (Anthropic)"

; Axiom 7 on the midlines: every common tangent would land .a or .c beside
; the part of its line that lies on the paper, so no fold carries out both
; alignments (ADR 0031). A program that wants such a landing constructs the
; target line first.

paper square
mark (map .a onto .b) as --v
mark (map .a onto .d) as --h
fold (map .a onto --v and .c onto --h)

; expect error "no fold of map .a onto --v and .c onto --h carries out all its alignments at once"
